                                "sense_id": "559bfc81-2086-3d2c-bd48-e051b81f6fbc",
                                "text": "Besides the wind, sand, tumbleweed, and Joshua trees, there was nothing at Muroc except for two quonset-style hangars, side by side, a couple of gasoline pumps, a single concrete runway, a few tarpaper shacks, and some tents."
